About the Opportunity
The Technical Services Team guides clients through the lifecycle of delivering third party flat file integrations as part of an overall Dayforce HCM implementation.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Our team helps clients achieve a positive go-live experience by coordinating key internal and external stakeholders to complete activities that will allow clients to be able to transmit business-critical data (benefits enrollment, COBRA, payroll contribution, HR demographic) to their vendors when they go live with their new HCM system.&nbsp;
You will be part of a specific business segment team, or pod, comprised of Consultants working on client implementation projects across North America. You will be supported by experts in each file type in your pod as well as having access to our larger team&rsquo;s expertise. Our Technical Services group is connected by a sense of camaraderie; we are grounded in a sense of belonging and a supportive remote-work culture. &nbsp;
We are looking for experienced Consultants who can concurrently manage multiple files across multiple implementation projects -- people who are confident, agile, and proactive.&nbsp;
What You&rsquo;ll Get to Do

Provide consulting services to clients&nbsp;&nbsp;
Translate client requirements into flat file requirements&nbsp; 
Meet with offshore teams to review the mapping document for file development 
Manage internal (Project Managers, Project Sponsors, Service Consultants, Mappers) and external (Clients and Vendors) stakeholders to achieve export file deliverables 
Identify and communicate risk&nbsp; 
Analyze export files and research the cause of the issue to determine course of action 
Responsible for the end-to-end management of delivering export files&nbsp;&nbsp;

Skills and Experience We Value

Bachelor&rsquo;s degree or equivalent experience 
5+ years of experience in human capital management consulting 
Client relationship acumen  
Ability to engage with multiple projects &amp; clients concurrently and manage priorities 
Excellent organizational, communication, collaboration, and consulting skills 
Ability to lead and facilitate client workshops and sessions 
Ability to relay technical concepts to clients in clear and concise business language&nbsp; 
Understanding of common human capital management (HCM) business practices&nbsp;&nbsp;

What Would Make You Really Stand Out

Project management exposure&nbsp; 
Experience with software in a SaaS / Cloud computing environment including experience with HRIS Systems&nbsp; 
Good working knowledge of payroll contribution, benefits eligibility, and HR files&nbsp; 
Ability to read a technical specification from a vendor and analyze vendor feedback&nbsp;&nbsp;

Location:&nbsp;Work is what you do, not where you go.&nbsp;For this role, we are open to remote work and can hire anywhere in Australia and New Zealand
&nbsp;
About the opportunity
&nbsp;
The aPay Dayforce Service Consultant participates in all stages of the aPay implementation lifecycle (discovery, configuration, testing, deployment, post-go-live support) under the direction of the Project Manager and may lead one or more of these activities to design and delivery quality payroll solutions to Dayforce customers.
&nbsp;
What you&rsquo;ll get to do&nbsp;
&nbsp;

Document and validate customer business requirements and map them to aPay Dayforce functionality.
Design and document innovative solutions to address customer business needs.
Configure aPay Dayforce modules to meet customers documented business requirements.
Conduct consulting sessions (over the phone and in-person) and document them with meeting minutes.
Actively participate in customer testing cycles, promptly addressing and resolving any identified issues.
Attend internal project meetings and provide status updates on the progress of activities and deliverables.
Provide customers with follow-up consulting and general assistance in areas of expertise.
Serve as a &ldquo;go-to&rdquo; resource for specific functional areas for both internal and external users.

&nbsp;
Skills and experience we value&nbsp;
&nbsp;

Bachelor&rsquo;s degree or equivalent experience
5 to 7 years&rsquo; experience in a Software Implementation role or 5+ Experience with payroll or related HR systems an advantage; experience with Ascender Pay preferred but not required.
Experience with software design and implementation, including document writing experience.
Excellent analytical skills, creative and critical thinking with the ability to make decisions on the job to achieve project outcomes.
Excellent communication skills (high level of written and verbal) with experience consulting to external clients.
Organized and able to schedule and prioritize time with the ability to work under pressure and deliver to project deadlines.
Ability to work autonomously or as part of a project team.

&nbsp;
What would make you really stand out&nbsp;
&nbsp;

Motivated to work with minimal supervision
Desire to achieve set goals
Prepared to work extraordinary hours when required to keep projects back on track
Ability to deal with clients at all levels
Maintain a positive attitude towards your work and other staff
Respect the wishes of the customer always maintaining a polite attitude
Desire to treat others, as you would prefer to be treated

&nbsp;

